# Optional untracked overrides. Copy to config/site.local.conf only when the
# automatic local/Nikhef profile is not sufficient.
#
# setupEnv.sh sources this file INSTEAD of config/sites/<site>.conf, so none of
# the tracked profile's refusals run, and nothing this file leaves unset gets a
# site default. Set every root you need, not only the data root. setupEnv.sh
# then checks each resolved root and stops when one is empty, relative, carries
# an empty path segment, ends with a separator, carries a . or .. segment, or
# contains a newline.
#
# Use the ": ${NAME:=value}" form. setupEnv.sh documents the precedence as
# environment > local > tracked defaults, and only that form honours it; a plain
# NAME=value assignment silently overrides an exported value instead.
#
# Write a literal path. Never build a path segment from the environment:
# tools/render_production_submit.py emits `getenv = False` and no
# `environment =` line, so a Condor job starts with an empty environment.
# ${USER} was empty on the execute node, /data/alice//hf collapsed to the shared
# /data/alice/hf, and the first HF_SMOKE3 pilot wrote outside the account
# because that path still resolved.
#
# : "${HADRONIZATION_SITE:=nikhef}"
# : "${HADRONIZATION_DATA_ROOT:=/data/alice/my-account/hf}"
# : "${HF_PRODUCTION_ROOT:=/another/large/storage/hadronization_production}"
